  "summary": "Locates an address in the buddy allocator: its zone, its free block, and where it sits inside that block.",
  "usage": "kernlens-buddy [-h] [-z ZONE] [-o ORDER] [-m MTYPE] [-n NODE] [-v]\n                      [--limit LIMIT]\n                      [command ...]",
  "examples": "kl-buddy list -o 10\nkl-buddy info 0xffff8880032a1000\nkl-buddy info pfn:0x7400 -v\nkl-buddy freelist -o 10 -m Movable -v",
  "notes": "`inf`o` accepts a virtual address, a physical address, a `struct page` address, or a `pfn:`/`phys:`/`page:`/`virt:` prefixed value.  The order comes from the block head's `private` field, which the kernel only maintains while a block is free; an allocated page reports `Order: -`.",
